The conda packages produced by this repository bundle the ESA Sentinel Application
Platform (SNAP) and its SAR toolboxes:

  - SNAP (snap-engine, snap-desktop)
  - Sentinel-1 Toolbox (s1tbx)
  - Radar/Polarimetric Toolbox (rstb)

SNAP is developed by the European Space Agency (ESA) and contributors, including
Brockmann Consult GmbH, SkyWatch, and CS Group, and is distributed under the
GNU General Public License, version 3 (GPL-3.0). Bundled third-party components
are listed with their individual licenses in THIRDPARTY_LICENSES.txt (shipped
inside each package under opt/snap/).

The packages contain a PRUNED SUBSET of the official ESA SNAP "sentinel"
distribution (the optical Sentinel-2/3 toolboxes and the bundled JRE are removed);
SNAP's source code is redistributed UNMODIFIED. Corresponding source (GPL-3.0 §6)
is available at https://github.com/senbox-org using the release tag matching the
packaged version. A written offer for the corresponding source is available via
https://github.com/pmuguda/snap-gpt-conda .

